    "['ip dhcp pool [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services dhcp-local-server group pool1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system services dhcp-local-server group pool1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `ip dhcp pool pool1` command:\\n\\n##\\nset system services dhcp-local-server group pool1\\nset system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 address-range low 10.10.10.0 high 10.10.10.255\\nset system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 default-lease-time 86400\\nset system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 router 10.10.10.1\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper handles DHCP configuration differently than Cisco. The above commands:\\n1. Create a DHCP server group named \"pool1\"\\n2. Define the address range (equivalent to Cisco\\'s network statement)\\n3. Set a default lease time (86400 seconds = 1 day, which is typical if not specified)\\n4. Configure the default router option\\n\\nThe lease time is included because Juniper requires it, while Cisco uses a default when not specified.', 'trans_template': 'set system services dhcp-local-server group pool1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 address-range low 10.10.10.0 high 10.10.10.255', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 address-range low 10.10.10.0 high 10.10.10.255', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `ip dhcp pool pool1` command:\\n\\n##\\nset system services dhcp-local-server group pool1\\nset system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 address-range low 10.10.10.0 high 10.10.10.255\\nset system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 default-lease-time 86400\\nset system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 router 10.10.10.1\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper handles DHCP configuration differently than Cisco. The above commands:\\n1. Create a DHCP server group named \"pool1\"\\n2. Define the address range (equivalent to Cisco\\'s network statement)\\n3. Set a default lease time (86400 seconds = 1 day, which is typical if not specified)\\n4. Configure the default router option\\n\\nThe lease time is included because Juniper requires it, while Cisco uses a default when not specified.', 'trans_template': 'set system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 address-range low 10.10.10.0 high 10.10.10.255'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 default-lease-time 86400', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 default-lease-time 86400', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `ip dhcp pool pool1` command:\\n\\n##\\nset system services dhcp-local-server group pool1\\nset system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 address-range low 10.10.10.0 high 10.10.10.255\\nset system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 default-lease-time 86400\\nset system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 router 10.10.10.1\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper handles DHCP configuration differently than Cisco. The above commands:\\n1. Create a DHCP server group named \"pool1\"\\n2. Define the address range (equivalent to Cisco\\'s network statement)\\n3. Set a default lease time (86400 seconds = 1 day, which is typical if not specified)\\n4. Configure the default router option\\n\\nThe lease time is included because Juniper requires it, while Cisco uses a default when not specified.', 'trans_template': 'set system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 default-lease-time 86400'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 router 10.10.10.1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 router 10.10.10.1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `ip dhcp pool pool1` command:\\n\\n##\\nset system services dhcp-local-server group pool1\\nset system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 address-range low 10.10.10.0 high 10.10.10.255\\nset system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 default-lease-time 86400\\nset system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 router 10.10.10.1\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper handles DHCP configuration differently than Cisco. The above commands:\\n1. Create a DHCP server group named \"pool1\"\\n2. Define the address range (equivalent to Cisco\\'s network statement)\\n3. Set a default lease time (86400 seconds = 1 day, which is typical if not specified)\\n4. Configure the default router option\\n\\nThe lease time is included because Juniper requires it, while Cisco uses a default when not specified.', 'trans_template': 'set system services dhcp-local-server group pool1 router 10.10.10.1'}]]": 1,
    "['network [parameter1] [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services dhcp pool pool1 address-range low 10.10.10.1 high 10.10.10.254', 'parent_command': ['set system services dhcp-local-server group pool1'], 'root': 'set system services dhcp-local-server group pool1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco DHCP pool network configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset system services dhcp pool pool1 address-range low 10.10.10.1 high 10.10.10.254\\nset system services dhcp pool pool1 default-router 10.10.10.1\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper handles DHCP configuration differently than Cisco. While Cisco uses the `network` command to define both the subnet and implied range, Juniper requires explicit address range specification (typically excluding the network and broadcast addresses). The default-router configuration is maintained separately in Juniper's DHCP pool configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'set system services dhcp pool pool1 address-range low 10.10.10.1 high 10.10.10.254'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services dhcp pool pool1 default-router 10.10.10.1', 'parent_command': ['set system services dhcp-local-server group pool1'], 'root': 'set system services dhcp-local-server group pool1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco DHCP pool network configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset system services dhcp pool pool1 address-range low 10.10.10.1 high 10.10.10.254\\nset system services dhcp pool pool1 default-router 10.10.10.1\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper handles DHCP configuration differently than Cisco. While Cisco uses the `network` command to define both the subnet and implied range, Juniper requires explicit address range specification (typically excluding the network and broadcast addresses). The default-router configuration is maintained separately in Juniper's DHCP pool configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'set system services dhcp pool pool1 default-router 10.10.10.1'}]]": 1,
    "['default-router [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set forwarding-options dhcp-relay server-group pool1 10.10.10.1', 'parent_command': ['set system services dhcp-local-server group pool1'], 'root': 'set system services dhcp-local-server group pool1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `default-router` DHCP configuration command:\\n\\n##\\nset forwarding-options dhcp-relay server-group pool1 10.10.10.1\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, the exact equivalent depends on the context. For a DHCP server configuration (rather than relay), you would typically use:\\n```\\nset system services dhcp pool pool1 default-router 10.10.10.1\\n```\\nThe first translation I provided assumes a DHCP relay scenario, which is more common in service provider environments. The second shows the direct DHCP server equivalent. Choose based on your specific implementation context.\", 'trans_template': 'set forwarding-options dhcp-relay server-group pool1 10.10.10.1'}]]": 1,
    "['ipv6 unicast-routing', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-options rib inet6.0 static', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set routing-options rib inet6.0 static', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset routing-options rib inet6.0 static\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you're using a more modern Junos version (where IPv6 unicast routing is enabled by default), you might simply need:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols router-advertisement interface all\\n##\\n\\nNote: The first translation creates an IPv6 routing table explicitly. The second enables router advertisements which implies IPv6 routing capability. Junos typically has IPv6 routing enabled by default, so often no explicit command is needed (unlike Cisco which requires `ipv6 unicast-routing` to enable it).\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-options rib inet6.0 static'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset routing-options rib inet6.0 static\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you're using a more modern Junos version (where IPv6 unicast routing is enabled by default), you might simply need:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols router-advertisement interface all\\n##\\n\\nNote: The first translation creates an IPv6 routing table explicitly. The second enables router advertisements which implies IPv6 routing capability. Junos typically has IPv6 routing enabled by default, so often no explicit command is needed (unlike Cisco which requires `ipv6 unicast-routing` to enable it).\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all'}]]": 1,
    "['ipv6 dhcp pool [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set system services dhcp-local-server dhcpv6 group pool1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set system services dhcp-local-server dhcpv6 group pool1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `ipv6 dhcp pool` command:\\n\\n##\\nset system services dhcp-local-server dhcpv6 group pool1\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper command establishes a DHCPv6 server group, but you'll need additional configuration to fully match the Cisco functionality (such as prefix delegation parameters). The Cisco configuration shows a commented-out prefix delegation (`address prefix`), which would need separate Juniper commands like `set system services dhcp-local-server dhcpv6 group pool1 dynamic-profile` if implemented.\", 'trans_template': 'set system services dhcp-local-server dhcpv6 group pool1'}]]": 1,
